axtwo$ & $\\rgamatxtwo$ & $\\gamaR$   \\\\\r\n  $2\\rgamawtwo-1$\\,$^*$  & $2\\rgamatwo-1$\\,$^*$    & $\\rgamaxtwo$ & $\\rgamatxtwo$ & $2\\gamaR-2$\\,$^*$    \\\\\r\n  & $2\\rgamawtwo$ & $2\\rgamatwo$ & 2$\\rgamaxtwo$ & $\\rgamatxtwo$ & $2\\gamaR$\\\\\r\n9 & $\\rgamawtwo$ & $2\\gama$ & $2\\gamat$  &  $2\\gamawtwo-2$ & $2\\gamasettwo-2$ &$2\\gamatsettwo-2$ & $2\\gamatwo-2$ & $2\\gamaxtwo-2$ & $2\\gamatxtwo-2$ & $=$ &  $\\rgamatwo$  & $\\rgamaxtwo$ &\n<truncated 2144 bytes>\n\\rgamatwo(F_n^4)\\le n+1$, which is proven by\r\nthe inequality $\\rgamawtwo(F_n^4)\\le \\rgamatwo(F_n^4)$ (see Table \\ref{table-bounds}) and the function\r\nThe values $\\gamawtwo(F_n^4)=\\gamatwo(F_n^4)=\\rgamawtwo(F_n^4)=\\rgamatwo(F_n^4)=n+1$\r\n\\multicolumn{2}{|c||}{} &  $\\gamma$ & $\\gamat$ & $\\gamawtwo$ & $\\gamasettwo$ & $\\gamatsettwo$ & $\\gamatwo$ & $\\gamaxtwo$ & $\\gamatxtwo$   & $\\rgamawtwo$ & $\\rgamatwo$ & $\\rgamaxtwo$ & $\\rgamatxtwo$ &  $\\gamaR$   \\\\\r\n9 & $\\rgamawtwo$ & $kK_2$ & $kH$  & $K_n^{**},n\\ge 3$  &\r\nSince the parameters $\\gama,\\gamat,\\gamawtwo,\\gamasettwo,\\rgamawtwo,\\gamaR$\r\nWe are not aware of inapproximability results for any of the invariants \\hbox{$\\rho\\in \\{\\gamaR, \\gamawtwo, \\gamasettwo, \\gamatsettwo, \\rgamatwo, \\rgamawtwo, \\rgamaxtwo, \\rgamatxtwo\\}$.} (Recall that invariants $\\rgamatwo$, $\\rgamaxtwo$, and $\\rgamatxtwo$ are, to the best of our knowledge, considered for the first time in this paper.) The following \\NP-completeness results for some of these parameters are available in the literature:\r\n  \\item The weak $2$-domination ($\\gamawtwo$) and the rainbow weak $2$-domination ($\\rgamawtwo$) problems were proved \\NP-complete by Bre\\v{s}ar and Kraner \\v{S}umenjak in~\\cite{bks-2007}.\r\n\\hbox{$\\rho\\in \\{\\gamawtwo, \\gamasettwo, \\gamatsettwo, \\gamaR, \\rgamatwo, \\rgamawtwo, \\rgamaxtwo\\}$,} it suffices to show an inapproximability bound of the same type for just one parameter in each of the bottom three equivalence classes\r\nFor every $\\rho\\in \\{\\gamawtwo, \\gamasettwo, \\gamatsettwo, \\gamaR, \\rgamawtwo, \\rgamasettwo, \\rgamatsettwo\\}$ and every $\\epsilon >0$, there is no polynomial time algorithm approximating $\\rho$ for $n$-vertex split graphs without isolated vertices within a factor of \\hbox{$(1/2-\\epsilon)\\ln n$}, {unless ${\\sf P} = {\\sf NP}$.}\r\n$\\gama(G)\\le \\gamawtwo(G)\\le \\rgamawtwo(G)\\le\\gamaR(G)\\le \\rgamasettwo(G) = 2\\gama(G)$ and\r\nFor every $\\rho\\in \\{\\gamasettwo, \\gamatsettwo, \\rgamawtwo, \\gamaR, \\rgamasettwo, \\rgamatsettwo\\}$, there is a $2(\\ln(\\Delta(G)+2)+1)$-approximation algorithm for $\\rho$.\r\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":83,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:38:49Z","thinking":"**Deriving Gamma Inequality Relations**\n\nExamining the provided inequalities, a relationship between different gamma values is evident. Specifically, line 2872 establishes several inequalities:  γ(G) ≤ γ̃w2(G) ≤ Rγ̃w2(G) ≤ γR(G) ≤ Rγset2(G) = 2γ(G).\n\nReviewing Proposition 2.1 reveals that γt(G) ≤ γ̃w2(G) ≤ γR(G). This implies that γt(G) is less than or equal to γR(G).\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\nimport urllib.request\\n\\n# Let's search for the text of Furuya's paper\\n# DOI: 10.1016/j.dam.2014.11.002\\n# Let's check unpaywall or sciencedirect or arxiv\\nurl = 'https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.1016/j.dam.2014.11.002?email=researcher@university.edu'\\nreq = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0'})\\ntry:\\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:\\n        import json\\n        data = json.loads(resp.read().decode('utf-8'))\\n        print('best_oa_location:', data.get('best_oa_location'))\\nexcept Exception as e:\\n    print('Error:', e)\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Querying unpaywall for Furuya paper\"","toolSummary":"\"Query unpaywall\""}}]}
