{"step_index":143,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:40:52Z","thinking":"**Evaluating Dominance and Budget**\n\nConsidering if a test set $S_{test}$ dominates $V_1$. A vertex $v$ in $V_1$ might not have a neighbor in $V_2$ that is also in $S_{test}$. If a vertex $v \\in V_1$ has no neighbor in $S_{test}$, what implications does this have? The function $f(v) = 1$ adds to the budget. The total budget is $2|V_2| + |V_1|$. In $S_{test}$, vertices used are at most $|V_2| + |I_2| \\le 2|V_2|$. No budget of $|V_1|$ has been used.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport itertools\\n\\n# Let's test on small graphs\\nfor n in range(2, 7):\\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\\n        if G.number_of_nodes() != n or any(G.degree(v) == 0 for v in G.nodes()):\\n            continue\\n        nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n        for f_tup in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\n            f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tup))\\n            if not all(f[v] > 0 or any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\\n                continue\\n            w = sum(f_tup)\\n            V0 = [v for v in nodes if f[v] == 0]\\n            V1 = [v for v in nodes if f[v] == 1]\\n            V2 = [v for v in nodes if f[v] == 2]\\n            \\n            # Let's see: what total dominating sets exist?\\n            # Check how close V2 + neighbors is\\n            pass\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Python test setup\"","toolSummary":"\"Python test setup\""}}]}
